WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.867 --> 00:00:19.316
"I know why someone would take the movie tickets but not these games," Cole said.

2
00:00:19.317 --> 00:00:22.804
"It's simple. The thief stumbled across that plastic container.

3
00:00:22.805 --> 00:00:25.557
But he didn't find this treasure chest."

4
00:00:25.558 --> 00:00:31.103
"Yeah," Luke agreed. "William's parents said that's probably what happened."

5
00:00:31.104 --> 00:00:35.647
"I still think Roger Redbeard stole our tickets," Maggie added.

6
00:00:35.648 --> 00:00:39.182
"He probably didn't notice the clue in the box."

7
00:00:39.183 --> 00:00:43.809
"It's a good thing he didn't know about this booty," Nathan said.

8
00:00:43.810 --> 00:00:47.688
"We wouldn't have our awesome new game players right now!"

9
00:00:47.689 --> 00:00:49.910
Henry didn't say anything.

10
00:00:49.911 --> 00:01:00.404
He still wasn't sure that Roger was the thief. They needed more evidence.

11
00:01:00.405 --> 00:01:04.147
Henry was still thinking as they started to walk back to the beach.

12
00:01:04.148 --> 00:01:07.730
He had to find out if Roger had really walked to town.

13
00:01:07.731 --> 00:01:09.445
"Hey, Anna," he said.

14
00:01:09.446 --> 00:01:14.375
"Did you see Roger walking by the surf while we were all checking the tide pools?"

15
00:01:14.376 --> 00:01:18.291
Anna blinked. "Excuse me?" she said.

16
00:01:18.292 --> 00:01:20.598
Henry repeated his question.

17
00:01:20.599 --> 00:01:25.544
She shook her head. "I didn't go down by the surf," she replied.

18
00:01:25.545 --> 00:01:28.607
"My tide pool wasn't close to the water."

19
00:01:28.608 --> 00:01:30.871
"Really?" Maggie said.

20
00:01:30.872 --> 00:01:34.697
"Because Roger said he saw you running through the surf."

21
00:01:34.698 --> 00:01:39.220
"He did?" Anna said. Then she gave a quick smile.

22
00:01:39.221 --> 00:01:45.577
"Oh, I know. I bet he saw my sister. She's only two years older than I am.

23
00:01:45.578 --> 00:01:49.946
A lot of people think we look alike. She was probably jogging.

24
00:01:49.947 --> 00:01:52.543
She loves to exercise."

25
00:01:52.544 --> 00:01:55.044
Henry thought of another question for Anna.

26
00:01:55.045 --> 00:01:58.433
"How long does it take to walk to town from here?"

27
00:01:58.434 --> 00:02:02.363
"About fifteen or twenty minutes," Anna replied.

28
00:02:02.364 --> 00:02:05.382
Cole wasn't paying much attention to the conversation.

29
00:02:05.383 --> 00:02:07.812
He was staring at the next clue.

30
00:02:07.813 --> 00:02:13.246
"It's a drawing of some buildings," he said. "Close to a park or something."

31
00:02:13.247 --> 00:02:16.086
"I think we have to go into town," said Luke.

32
00:02:16.087 --> 00:02:20.030
"We can play our games on the way."

33
00:02:20.031 --> 00:02:23.412
Everyone started walking up the beach toward town.

34
00:02:23.413 --> 00:02:26.831
When they passed William's house, William stopped.

35
00:02:26.832 --> 00:02:30.404
"I'll catch up with you in a few minutes," he said.

36
00:02:30.405 --> 00:02:37.329
"These sandals are giving me blisters. I want to put on different ones."

37
00:02:37.330 --> 00:02:42.255
Without waiting for an answer, he ran ahead and disappeared into his house.

38
00:02:42.256 --> 00:02:44.719
The others stared after him.

39
00:02:44.720 --> 00:02:49.190
"What's wrong with William today?" Nathan said with a frown.

40
00:02:49.191 --> 00:02:54.356
"He seems grouchy. It's almost like he wishes we weren't here."

41
00:02:54.357 --> 00:03:01.398
Henry had been thinking the same thing. He just shrugged. "I'm not sure."

42
00:03:01.399 --> 00:03:03.180
They all kept walking.

43
00:03:03.181 --> 00:03:07.233
Everyone except Henry was focused on their video game players.

44
00:03:07.234 --> 00:03:12.799
Soon Henry poked Cole and Maggie, gesturing for them to slow down.

45
00:03:12.800 --> 00:03:18.782
He wanted The Lemonade Detectives to whisper to one another without anyone else overhearing.

46
00:03:18.783 --> 00:03:22.701
"What do you guys think?" Henry asked quietly.

47
00:03:22.702 --> 00:03:28.616
"If Roger really walked to town and back, it took him at least half an hour."

48
00:03:28.617 --> 00:03:34.654
"Plus however long it took him to go into a store and buy that soda," Cole pointed out.

49
00:03:34.655 --> 00:03:39.393
"That means he didn't have time to steal our tickets," Maggie added.

50
00:03:39.394 --> 00:03:42.642
"If he's telling the truth, that is."

51
00:03:42.643 --> 00:03:46.126
Cole nodded. "We still don't know for sure.

52
00:03:46.127 --> 00:03:48.532
Anna said she didn't see him, remember?"

53
00:03:48.533 --> 00:03:55.282
"I know." Henry glanced forward to make sure the others weren't listening.

54
00:03:55.283 --> 00:04:00.879
"When we get to town, let's try to find out if he really bought that soda there."

55
00:04:00.880 --> 00:04:04.181
"How are we going to do that?" Cole asked.

56
00:04:04.182 --> 00:04:10.193
"There was a logo on the cup," Henry replied. "It said SCGS.

57
00:04:10.194 --> 00:04:13.447
Maybe we can find a business with that name."

58
00:04:13.448 --> 00:04:17.918
"Okay," Cole said. "But what about our other suspects?"

59
00:04:17.919 --> 00:04:21.181
"Like William, for instance," Maggie said.

60
00:04:21.182 --> 00:04:24.692
"It's pretty suspicious that he ran off by himself."

61
00:04:24.693 --> 00:04:28.286
"This is the second time he's done that," Cole said.

62
00:04:28.287 --> 00:04:32.183
"He left when he and I were supposed to be searching together too."

63
00:04:32.184 --> 00:04:35.572
"That is suspcious," Henry agreed.

64
00:04:35.573 --> 00:04:40.564
"We should pay attention to William. And to Anna, Luke, and Nathan."

65
00:04:40.565 --> 00:04:44.717
"I still don't think Nathan would steal anything," Cole said.

66
00:04:44.718 --> 00:04:48.443
"I know he's acting kind of grouchy today, but—"

67
00:04:48.444 --> 00:04:54.610
Cole stopped short. Henry saw why. Luke was dropping back to join them.

68
00:04:54.611 --> 00:04:57.887
"Keep up, you guys," he said with a smile.

69
00:04:57.888 --> 00:05:01.464
"Otherwise we might not share the next pirate booty with you!"

70
00:05:01.465 --> 00:05:06.913
Henry chuckled. Since Luke was there, he decided to try to question him.

71
00:05:06.914 --> 00:05:11.310
"It's too bad about those missing movie tickets, huh?" he said.

72
00:05:11.311 --> 00:05:16.341
"You're such a big fan of pirates, I bet you'd love to go to that premiere."

73
00:05:16.342 --> 00:05:20.178
Luke didn't answer. Henry looked over at him.

74
00:05:20.179 --> 00:05:23.299
To Henry's surprise, Luke wasn't smiling anymore.

75
00:05:23.300 --> 00:05:26.024
His face was turning bright red.

76
00:05:26.025 --> 00:05:30.317
"Um, actually, about those movie tickets . . ." Luke muttered.

77
00:05:30.318 --> 00:05:36.192
Henry's eyes widened. Was Luke about to confess to the crime?
